---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE, pathFor } from '../../../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title="How to make a Kiss Cam clip from two photos"
  description="Step-by-step Kiss Cam AI: two adult-consent photos, credits, ~11–12s stadium-style remix — no Coldplay concert footage."
  canonicalPath="/blog/how-to-make-kiss-cam-from-two-photos/"
  ogType="article"
>
  <article class="section wrap prose">
    <p class="meta">Published 2026-10-21 · Updated 2026-10-23 · ~8 min</p>
    <h1>How to make a Kiss Cam clip from two photos</h1>
    <p>
      “Coldplay Kiss Cam” style clips mimic a stadium jumbotron moment. On this site the template is
      <strong>Coldplay Kiss Cam AI</strong> — a <strong>two-photo</strong> AI remix, not official Coldplay content and
      <strong>not real concert footage</strong>. Create UI:
      <a href={pathFor('en', '/create/kiss-cam/')}>/create/kiss-cam/</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="callout warn">
      <strong>Compliance.</strong> Adults (18+) or pets only. Confirm permission. Not affiliated with Coldplay, CapCut, or any venue.
    </div>

    <h2>Step-by-step checklist</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Pick Photo A and Photo B</strong> — two clear subjects (people or pets). Same lighting helps; not required.</li>
      <li><strong>Open Create</strong> — go to the Kiss Cam path (not Bby Wow / Ceiling Fan — those are 1-photo UIs).</li>
      <li><strong>Upload both slots</strong> — JPG/PNG/WebP, roughly under 10MB each.</li>
      <li><strong>Check the consent box</strong> — adults or pets; AI remix disclaimer.</li>
      <li><strong>Spend 1 credit</strong> — one-shot listed at ${SITE.pricing.kissCamOneShotUsd} on <a href={pathFor('en', '/pricing/')}>Pricing</a> (Waffo stub until <code>WAFFO_*</code>).</li>
      <li><strong>Generate</strong> — target length ~11–12s vertical. Without <code>FAL_*</code>, the UI demos a queued job.</li>
      <li><strong>Download / share</strong> — add licensed audio yourself if needed; we claim no Coldplay (or other) song license.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Why two photos (not one)?</h2>
    <p>
      The meme’s punchline is the <em>pair</em> on the big screen — lean-in, dodge, or kiss. A single portrait cannot stage both subjects.
      That is why the wall routes Kiss Cam to a dual-slot uploader while Bby Wow and Ceiling Fan stay single-slot.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do <em>not</em> do</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Claim sometimes seen in SERPs</th><th>Our policy (2026-10)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>“Official Coldplay filter”</td><td>False — independent AI remix</td></tr>
          <tr><td>“Uses concert night footage”</td><td>False — no real concert footage</td></tr>
          <tr><td>“Includes the song license”</td><td>False — audio is your responsibility</td></tr>
          <tr><td>“Works with minors”</td><td>Prohibited</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Photo tips</h2>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Faces unobscured; avoid heavy filters that break identity.</li>
      <li>Pets: full body or clear face; you must have permission to depict them.</li>
      <li>Do not upload celebrities you do not have rights to commercially exploit.</li>
      <li>Expect ~{SITE.photoRetentionDays}-day retention then deletion (Privacy).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Failed jobs</h2>
    <p>
      If generation fails after debit due to pipeline/provider error, we refund the credit / one-shot
      (see <a href={pathFor('en', '/terms/')}>Terms</a> / <a href={pathFor('en', '/faq/')}>FAQ</a>).
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top:2rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={pathFor('en', '/create/kiss-cam/')}>Create Kiss Cam</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={pathFor('en', '/blog/what-is-bby-wow-ai/')} style="margin-left:0.5rem">Related: Bby Wow</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
